Subject: Cantor Attention Manifest Refresh P6 Projection Cost Measurement

@ [research_uuid] d46f44d6-cca2-411f-8aa7-ee253c23ec58
@ [measurement_date] 2026-09-02
@ [implementation_commit] b08837ae0bdb56c27c4adc3786b07b2e72072cd5

& [Question]
  + does the complete compact manifest materially reduce inference-window bytes while preserving exact basket membership rather than merely renaming the full register

& [Method]
  + compile the same valid frame and ledger through the legacy full register and P6 compact manifest
  + compare canonical UTF-8 rendered byte counts at one eight and thirty-two members
  + increase mutable body payload per member from 64 to 256 to 1024 bytes
  + require equal exact member counts and strictly increasing absolute reduction
  + inspect the compact rendering for absence of readiness maintenance differentiators and body-payload values

& [MeasuredResults]
  + [members_1_payload_64] manifest 466 bytes full register 791 bytes reduction 325 bytes about 41.1 percent
  + [members_8_payload_256] manifest 1964 bytes full register 6100 bytes reduction 4136 bytes about 67.8 percent
  + [members_32_payload_1024] manifest 7101 bytes full register 48221 bytes reduction 41120 bytes about 85.3 percent
  + [small_existing_fixture] manifest 892 bytes full register 1605 bytes reduction 713 bytes about 44.4 percent

& [Finding]
  + P6 is not only structurally cleaner; it separates identity cost from mutable-body richness so the advantage grows as exact records become larger
  + the manifest still grows linearly with member count because completeness is mandatory; it moves the dominant body cost behind explicit materialization rather than eliminating identity cost
  + exact labels handles types versions and digests remain visible while readiness state differentiators roles purposes obligations provenance and arbitrary body payload remain absent until selected

& [Implication]
  + the inference window can continuously carry the basket roster and pay exact body cost only for currently Relevant candidates
  + the next behavioral evaluation should compare identity swap omission and false-merge rates at equal context budgets rather than only compare byte size

& [Nonclaims]
  + these are deterministic canonical-byte measurements from synthetic fixtures not tokenizer counts model quality measurements production capacity claims or evidence of internal attention
